      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Understand this: in a democracy, the right to complain is earned through the duty to participate. If you refuse to cast your ballot, you willingly surrender your right to critique the outcome. You forfeit your seat at the table, and you can demand better from the board without ever having bothered to show up for the meeting. Let us be defined not by our grievances, but by our relentless, uncompromising action at the polls.\"",
      "source": "target",
